A||N||1||bHooper||Does the front Swaybar affect the allignment?||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||11-01-2000||03:18 PM||||I am rebuilding the suspension, but probably want change the swaybar until later.  Does the car require an alignment if you remove and replace the swaybar?<P>Also, which swaybar is the best to use, up front?<P>I am replacing all tie rod ends, ball joints, steering damper, and adding Eibach springs and poly bushings.  So far, I have spent a but load of money, so if I can hold off on the swaybar until later (and not have to pay for an additional alignment) that would be great!<P>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||11-01-2000||03:41 PM||||Addco   from <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cyberauto.com</A>   Nopi wants $30 more for the same part for the front and rear.. to answer your question .. NO it doens't effect the alignment. it does effect the body roll in a corner and will let your tires wear more on their respective center (camber determined) or if your really a hard driver.. but for tooling around no.. you won't have to get it re-aligned.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
